{
  "_record": {
    "what": "The defective reading, kept as the evidence for the fix. DO NOT diff a new run against this file.",
    "defect": "A joint bend was read as the difference between two swings, each taken in the plane of forward and up. That equals the true joint angle only while the limb stays in that plane, so it understated every out-of-plane bend. Worst on netball_deflect_high at 52.67 degrees.",
    "solvedAgainst": "braven-movement main 481afa8, before the elbow separation work in PR #4 landed at 828bf6c.",
    "exportedBy": "lane/tactics-contract before the rebase, when the branch tip carried the planar bend.",
    "twoThingsChangedSince": "the bend became the angle between the two segments, and the solve gained the elbow fix. Only the first of those is what this file is evidence of.",
    "currentBaseline": "clip-baseline.json"
  },
